The code statements that lead to the bug are:
session = l2tp_v2_session_get(net, tunnel_id, session_id);
if (version != tunnel->version)
    goto invalid;
Reason:
The session reference is acquired via `l2tp_v2_session_get()` (or `l2tp_v3_session_get()`), but when the protocol version does not match `tunnel->version`, the code jumps to `invalid` without calling `l2tp_session_put(session)`, causing a memory leak of the session, tunnel, and associated socket.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (version != tunnel->version) {
    l2tp_session_put(session);
    goto invalid;
}
Reason:
The fix adds `l2tp_session_put(session)` before the `goto invalid` in the version‑check branch, ensuring the session reference is properly released when a version mismatch is detected, thereby preventing the memory leak.

